      "short_id": "mgy3tr",
      "created_at": "2026-10-28T10:53:34.963-05:00",
      "title": "Pair-coding Lobste.rs feat",
      "url": "",
      "score": 8,
      "flags": 0,
      "comment_count": 2,
      "description": "<p>There is a long standing <a href=\"https://github.com/lobsters/lobsters/issues/1165\" rel=\"ugc\">issue</a> I'm <a href=\"https://github.com/lobsters/lobsters/pull/2229\" rel=\"ugc\">working at</a> that turned out to have some interesting refactoring suggested by the <a href=\"https://github.com/orgs/lobsters/people\" rel=\"ugc\">admins</a>. Does anybody want to pair-code this feat with me? (I also mentioned it in irc). I believe discussing the codebase would be incredibly helpful for me and others wiling to contribute to Lobsters. I'm not a super experienced programmer and I'm not sure yet how to organize this kind of pair-work but thought mentioning it here would be worth a shot and super fun thing to do :D</p>\n<p>PS: Of course <a href=\"https://github.com/lobsters/lobsters/blob/main/AGENTS.md\" rel=\"ugc\">no llm contribution is allowed</a>, just crude old style brain smashing! &lt;3</p>\n",
      "description_plain": "There is a long standing [issue](https://github.com/lobsters/lobsters/issues/1165) I'm [working at](https://github.com/lobsters/lobsters/pull/2229) that turned out to have some interesting refactoring suggested by the [admins](https://github.com/orgs/lobsters/people). Does anybody want to pair-code this feat with me? (I also mentioned it in irc). I believe discussing the codebase would be incredibly helpful for me and others wiling to contribute to Lobsters. I'm not a super experienced programmer and I'm not sure yet how to organize this kind of pair-work but thought mentioning it here would be worth a shot and super fun thing to do :D\r\n\r\nPS: Of course [no llm contribution is allowed](https://github.com/lobsters/lobsters/blob/main/AGENTS.md), just crude old style brain smashing! <3",
      "submitter_user": "rebeca",
      "user_is_author": true,
      "tags": [
